From: OfficeDroid contributors
Subject: [PATCH] wineandroid: use the public RGBA format for CPU presentation

The CPU bridge converts Wine BGRA pixels to the actual Android buffer format.
Request the public RGBA_8888 format for TextureView composition instead of the
legacy private BGRA format. Leave EGL's buffer format selection unchanged.
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like the modified Wine file.

--- a/dlls/wineandroid.drv/device.c
+++ b/dlls/wineandroid.drv/device.c
@@ -528,7 +528,7 @@
     data->hwnd = hwnd;
     data->opengl = opengl;
     if (!opengl) data->api = NATIVE_WINDOW_API_CPU;
-    data->buffer_format = PF_BGRA_8888;
+    data->buffer_format = opengl ? PF_BGRA_8888 : PF_RGBA_8888;
     data_map[idx] = data;
     for (i = 0; i < NB_CACHED_BUFFERS; i++) data->buffer_lru[i] = -1;
     return data;
